---
source: src/sql_snapshots.rs
---

[sqlite] retype a column
  ! SQLite cannot change a column's type, nullability or default in place.

[mysql] a partial index
  ! MySQL has no partial indexes.

[mariadb] a partial index
  ! MySQL has no partial indexes.

[mssql] replace a default
  ! SQL Server keeps a default as a named constraint, and its name is not read here.

[clickhouse] change nullability
  ! ClickHouse spells nullability in the type; edit the type to Nullable(…).

[postgres] drop the primary key's index
  ! A primary key's index is the key itself, which this editor does not change.

[mysql] drop the primary key's index
  ! A primary key's index is the key itself, which this editor does not change.

[mssql] drop the primary key's index
  ! A primary key's index is the key itself, which this editor does not change.
